[{:db/id -1 :doc/id "business-openrouter-provider-blockers-20260908" :doc/title "OpenRouter application blockers after fleet verification" :doc/as-of "2026-09-08" :source/dataset "business" :doc/body "# Application blockers after fleet sustained and cancellation checks\n\n2026-09-08. Primary: Murakumo fleet. Modal: matching-model stability backup only, with recovery-driven failback. Submission status remains not submitted; candidate is_ready remains false.\n\n## Closed or materially advanced\nAPI #241 merged bfe6f72c169c08aff6ea62046999162f206406ea; root pin 9f5215db877a743fbdd848fe3b2a38cfbc1ca535; deployed c1bd9bf9-66b2-458a-8873-81d31814c19e. The Worker now watches downstream writer closure and aborts upstream prefill without waiting for the next 15-second heartbeat. Built-artifact regression: old version fails specifically because origin abort is absent, new version passes while Request.signal remains un-aborted. Eight cancellation/admission/proxy tests, 25 catalog tests with 107 assertions and three native tests pass. The catalog now includes the verified upstream hugging_face_id Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B, observed live after deployment.\n\nBounded continuous public run, 08:37:46.288-08:42:39.762 UTC: 20 sequential pairs at 15-second cadence, 40/40 success, no 429, p95 elapsed 7090 ms, maximum 8278 ms. Actual duration 293.474 seconds. This is about five minutes of short prompts, not a peak-capacity benchmark or seven-day history. Load requests are in a separate ledger, not inserted into the normal soak ledger. SHA256 9f60a0b0c994e4df0373aa61a30f50d80344a27582d8be378de2bd497ae58669.\n\nLive cancellation at 08:44:58.318 UTC: first content was observed without DONE; the origin slot was busy; only the response body was cancelled, with the caller Request signal still not aborted. The slot became idle by 4168 ms after cancellation. Origin journal independently recorded cancel task id 56012 and release of that same task at n_tokens=259. This proves origin cancellation for this observed midstream request, not an instantaneous universal latency bound or restart recovery. Before-first-token cancellation is covered by the built-worker regression; a repeated live cold-prefill campaign is still unmeasured.\n\n## Remaining release/submission blockers\n1. Reliability and backup: finish long-duration observation, sustained parallel and long-context load, controlled backend stop/restart recovery, matching-model Modal failure routing, cooldown and failback. Existing Modal GLM-5.3-Flash does not substitute for Qwen3.8-27B. Verify a compatible backup and spend ceiling before activation. Separate fleet success from backup-rescued success; never recurse through OpenRouter. Owner's backup architecture is a product acceptance requirement, not a published OpenRouter mandate.\n2. Partner authorization and settlement: issue scoped partner credentials; establish durable, idempotent request/attempt attribution, complete streaming usage, cancellation/unknown treatment, atomic credit/reservation accounting and reconciliation to actual vendor and customer invoices. Offline #240 reconciliation is an aid, not deployed billing. Budget-estimate records are not actual invoices.\n3. Retention and public disclosures: final terms/privacy, actual Cloudflare logging, R2/Merkle history and deletion/compaction, accounting metadata and conditional Modal processing. API #243 enforces current-document content expiry on read for all job states, including completed jobs. This and the earlier source checks do not prove physical erasure or whole-service ZDR. Current draft legal pages are not a final partner data contract.\n4. Commercial identity and rights: owner-confirmed AWAI Network LLC and Newark business/support address; formation source documents now received (see document evidence below); current-status verification and billing contact; payment mechanism with OpenRouter (auto top-up or invoicing); applicable Modal terms or written permission for the backup resale scope. Do not equate a public company name with registration evidence. Modal management and billing access were verified in the later provider-evidence-refresh-20260908 report; the applicable Service Order remains unavailable. No vendor clarification sent.\n5. Unit economics and capacity: fleet cost per useful completed output plus measured backup incidence/cost, retries, idle capacity and edge fees; then set and validate offer price and sustainable capacity. Published Modal prices alone neither establish fleet cost nor prove a fleet offer is loss-making.\n\n## Timing versus hard eligibility\nSeven days / >=1000 non-429 samples / >=500 per mode / >=99.5% correctness / <=45-minute gaps are OUR internal low-volume qualification policy, not an OpenRouter-stated universal application waiting period. Earliest seven-day age remains 2026-09-15T05:39:47.525Z if coverage and counts pass. Do not claim readiness merely when the calendar reaches that time. About three hours of current observation cannot establish seven days.\nThe official provider requirements cover model catalog/identity, capabilities/prices/capacity and payment integration, among other operational fields. The catalog shape and upstream identity are now evidenced; partner settlement and truthful operational/commercial claims remain unresolved. An exploratory contact can describe these gaps, but is not an accepted production provider.\n\nPrimary source: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/community/for-providers\n\n\n## Contracting identity confirmed by owner — 2026-09-08\nLegal entity: AWAI Network, L.L.C. (formation certificate spelling). Business-account name: AWAI Network LLC.\nPublic business name: AWAI Network, L.L.C.\nBusiness website: https://awai.network/ .\nPreviously supplied business/support address: 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, United States. The later company-contact section distinguishes the Tokyo company address from this registered-office/support address.\nSource: owner-provided business-account information in this conversation. This confirms which entity the owner intends to contract through; it is not an independent registry lookup or proof of the signer's authority.\nThe owner states that EIN and other business information have been supplied to the account provider, but at that earlier stage no EIN value, state registration number, billing-contact email or support telephone was included. The document evidence below supersedes the missing formation and EIN-assignment evidence. Do not invent or publish these values. Do not reuse a historical registration number without verification. Obtain any sensitive identifier only if the actual onboarding process requires it, through its private channel.\nThe Modal invoice's junkawasakicom workspace label is not a different contracting entity declaration. Confirm the applicable Modal account agreement/Service Order against AWAI Network LLC. OpenRouter payment mechanism and billing contact remain open.\n\n\n## Document evidence supplied by owner — 2026-09-08\nReviewed all pages of the original PDFs using extraction and rendered-page inspection. The certificate states AWAI Network, L.L.C. as the formed legal name; use this exact spelling for legal contracting fields. AWAI Network LLC is the business-account and IRS spelling supplied by the owner.\nDelaware file number: 10704996. Formation filed July 20, 2026 at 4:24 p.m.; certified copy dated July 21, 2026. Registered office: 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, New Castle County, United States. Registered agent: Legalinc Corporate Services Inc. The formation page is signed Kawasaki Jun, Authorized Person. The owner separately designated this same address for business/support; the certificate itself describes a registered office, not a compute location.\nFormation source: /Users/junkawasaki/Downloads/AWAINetworkLLC - Approved Certificate of Formation.pdf (2 pages). SHA-256 bc9ceea6020138d27ebd5c1e1e9cbac0d1fbd3ba42185ee9a7f077a034f5db70.\nThe two files named AWAINetworkLLC - 147c Letter_Approved SS-4 (1).pdf and AWAINetworkLLC - 147c Letter_Approved SS-4 (3).pdf are byte-identical, each one page, SHA-256 4aef4648ba62ae421923603a0a794b843e92dd5cc4fceb91e3323ce112923c9f. They are an IRS EIN Unit fax dated August 5, 2026, naming AWAI Network LLC and recording an EIN assignment on that date. The EIN value was visually read but is deliberately not reproduced in this repository or public application narrative; consult the owner-supplied original privately when onboarding requires it.\nDespite their filenames, the visible document is not an approved SS-4 or a 147C letter. It expressly states that it is not the official EIN verification document and that a CP575 notice will follow. Record EIN assignment evidence as received, but do not mark official EIN verification documentation as received. If a counterparty requires that document, use an actual CP575 or 147C; do not assume every application requires one.\nThis resolves the earlier lack of source documents for formation/name/file number/registered office, and lack of an EIN assignment source. Document inspection is not an online Delaware authenticity/current-status check, independent IRS validation, proof of ownership or general contracting/signing authority. Billing contact, chosen payment rail and applicable Modal agreement remain separate open items. No documents or identifiers were transmitted externally; the application remains unsubmitted.\n\n\n## Company contact supplied by owner — 2026-09-08\nCompany-account name: AWAI Network LLC. Legal name on formation certificate: AWAI Network, L.L.C. Entity type: Delaware LLC. Formation date July 20, 2026; Delaware file number 10704996. The owner-supplied EIN matches the previously inspected IRS assignment fax; its value remains excluded from repository text and public application narrative.\nCompany representative: Kawasaki Jun (owner-confirmed role). Company telephone: +81 80 4280 1991, normalized +818042801991. Do not infer a separate billing contact or signing mandate solely from this field.\nCompany address, transcribed as supplied: postal code 150-0001; Tokyo; Shibuya; 2-2-39; Japan. Do not invent an omitted town/street or building name, or replace this company address with the registered office.\nDelaware registered office remains 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, United States, as supported by the formation certificate. The owner previously designated this same Newark address for customer support; retain it as the support address until changed. Keep company address, registered office, support address and compute/data-processing location as distinct fields.\nThis resolves the previously missing company representative, company telephone and company-address information through owner confirmation. It is not independent phone/address verification and does not turn the IRS assignment fax into CP575/147C. Billing email/contact designation, OpenRouter payment mechanism and applicable Modal agreement remain open. No account settings or public legal pages were changed, and no application was submitted.\n"}]
